{#-
Extractors:
  - response: AsIsExtractor()
-#}
{# SCENE HISTORY - lean triage prompt: history + draft only, no static/world context #}
{% set budget = max_tokens - 800 - count_tokens(draft) - count_tokens(guidance) %}
<|SECTION:SCENE|>
{% for scene_line in scene.context_history(budget=budget, min_dialogue=20, sections=False) -%}
{{ scene_line }}
{% endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
<|SECTION:DRAFT NARRATION|>
A smaller writing model has produced the following draft narration, intended to be appended to the current moment of the scene:

```draft
{{ draft }}
```
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
<|SECTION:TASK|>
You are triaging the draft before a possible full editorial review. Check it against the scene history:
- Repetition: does it repeat story beats, imagery, distinctive phrases or information that were already established?
- Stalling: does it fail to move the scene forward, merely re-describing the current state?
- Contradiction: does it conflict with established facts, characters, tone or the writing style?
{% if guidance %}
Additional review criteria:
{{ guidance }}
{% endif %}

This is a mechanical triage of fictional story text - judge only whether the draft needs editorial correction.

Respond with exactly one word: PASS if the draft is acceptable as-is, or ISSUES if it needs the full review.
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
